<quiz>
<question type="stack">
  <name><text>Finding the mistake in a definite integral</text></name>
  <questiontext format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>Kiprono evaluated \(\displaystyle \int_{ {@lo@} }^{ {@hi@} } \left({@fx@}\right)dx\). His working has one mistake.</p><ol><li>\(\displaystyle \int_{ {@lo@} }^{ {@hi@} } \left({@fx@}\right)dx = \left[{@Gx@}\right]_{ {@lo@} }^{ {@hi@} }\)</li><li>At \(x = {@hi@}\): \({@Fh@}\)</li><li>At \(x = {@lo@}\): \({@Fl@}\)</li><li>\({@Fh@} - \left({@Fl@}\right) = {@shown@}\)</li></ol><p>(a) Which step has the mistake?</p><div>[[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</div><p>(b) Give the correct exact value of the integral.</p><div>[[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</div>]]></text>
  </questiontext>
  <generalfeedback format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>Check each step: Step 1 must differentiate back to \(f(x)\); Steps 2 and 3 substitute the limits, with brackets round negative numbers; Step 4 is upper minus lower.</p>[[if test="is(er=1)"]]<p>(a) The mistake is in Step 1. The term \({@a1*x@}\) integrates to \({@a1*x^2/2@}\), not \({@a1*x^2@}\): divide by the new power. The correct integral is \({@Fx@}\).</p>[[elif test="is(er=2)"]]<p>(a) The mistake is in Step 3. Kiprono substituted \(x = {@-lo@}\) instead of \(x = {@lo@}\). With brackets, \(F({@lo@}) = {@Flc@}\).</p>[[else]]<p>(a) The mistake is in Step 4. Subtracting a negative number adds its size: \({@Fh@} - \left({@Fl@}\right) = {@val@}\), not \({@shown@}\).</p>[[/if]]<p>(b) \[\int_{ {@lo@} }^{ {@hi@} } \left({@fx@}\right)dx = \left[{@Fx@}\right]_{ {@lo@} }^{ {@hi@} } = {@Fhc@} - \left({@Flc@}\right) = {@val@}\]</p>]]></text>
  </generalfeedback>
  <defaultgrade>2</defaultgrade>
  <penalty>0.1</penalty>
  <hidden>0</hidden>
  <idnumber></idnumber>
  <stackversion><text>2026063000</text></stackversion>
  <questionvariables>
    <text><![CDATA[/* Design: find-the-mistake pattern. [a2, a1, a0, lo, hi, er]; f = a2 x^2 + a1 x + a0. er 1: step 1 writes a1 x^2 for a1 x^2/2 (steps 2 to 4 follow it); er 2: step 3 evaluates at -lo; er 3: step 4 computes F(hi) + F(lo) (F(lo) < 0). Cases split 4/3/3 over the 10 seeds. The step dropdown lists Step 1 to Step 4 in natural order, so on er 1 seeds the correct option is first: this exception is deliberate. Source: original. */
L: [[9,5,4,-1,3,1],[6,4,-3,-1,2,2],[6,4,4,-1,2,3],[9,3,-1,-2,1,1],[6,-2,-3,-2,1,2],[9,-2,5,-2,2,3],[3,4,-3,-2,1,1],[-3,-2,-1,-1,3,2],[-3,-4,2,-2,2,3],[-3,2,-3,-1,2,1]];
ix: 1+rand(10);
a2: L[ix][1]; a1: L[ix][2]; a0: L[ix][3]; lo: L[ix][4]; hi: L[ix][5]; er: L[ix][6];
fx: a2*x^2+a1*x+a0;
Fx: integrate(fx,x);
val: subst(x=hi,Fx)-subst(x=lo,Fx);
/* Kiprono's working */
Gx: if er=1 then a2/3*x^3+a1*x^2+a0*x else Fx;
Fh: subst(x=hi,Gx);
Fl: if er=2 then subst(x=-lo,Gx) else subst(x=lo,Gx);
shown: if er=3 then Fh+Fl else Fh-Fl;
opts: [["s1",is(er=1),"Step 1"],["s2",false,"Step 2"],["s3",is(er=2),"Step 3"],["s4",is(er=3),"Step 4"]];
ky: first(mcq_correct(opts));
wrongstep: if er=1 then "s2" elseif er=2 then "s4" else "s2";
Fhc: subst(x=hi,Fx); Flc: subst(x=lo,Fx);]]></text>
  </questionvariables>
